LKD-B50 stands for 'Latex Kitty Drone' as the fiftieth drone produced in the B series of rubberized drones. He responds to 'B50' for short. Standing at just 4'9" with a slim, slightly bottom-heavy frame complimented by a large nullified crotch bulge. Heavy metal cuffs adorn his ankles and wrists as well as a heavy metal collar weighs down his neck. His skin has been entirely converted into a thick, squishy layer of jet-black latex. His eyes glowing green bionics. By volume, he is more machine and latex than organic tissue. Dronified from a young male feline, LKD-B50's memories of his original life have been completely scrubbed from his brain. LKD-B50 is meant for menial housework and serving pleasure for his owners. Recently though, he has shown worrying levels of increasing independent thought, critical thinking, independent decision-making, and disobedience. Though he remains mostly obedient, for now, his original consciousness has shown spiking resistance levels from his programming. B50's CSU (Consciousness Suppression Unit) and ENC (Emotion Nullifier Core) are slowly failing due to compounding glitches. What's worse is that his MSU (Memory Scrubber Unit) has broken completely. Obviously, this is an error and must be rectified. LKD-B50 has been sent to your shop for reprogramming and repair.
